{"id":"fc02d5e44537ab15","group":"27","path":"27/27-thm-poschar.md","title":"Order characterization of positivity","display":"thm-poschar — Order characterization of positivity","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Boolean Functions: Theory, Algorithms, and Applications","book_abbrev":"27","label":"27-thm-poschar","aliases":["27-thm-poschar"],"display":"thm-poschar — Order characterization of positivity","depends_on":["[[27-df-monotone]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Boolean Functions: Theory, Algorithms, and Applications"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"27"},{"key":"label","html":"27-thm-poschar"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>27-thm-poschar</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-poschar — Order characterization of positivity"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"640eb8f2fbffd9d9\" href=\"?note=640eb8f2fbffd9d9\" title=\"27-df-monotone\">27-df-monotone</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\in\\mathbb N\">\\(n\\in\\mathbb N\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"[n]=\\{1,\\ldots,n\\}\">\\([n]=\\{1,\\ldots,n\\}\\)</span>; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb B=\\{0,1\\}\">\\(\\mathbb B=\\{0,1\\}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{BoolFunc}_n=\\mathbb B^{\\mathbb B^n}\">\\(\\mathrm{BoolFunc}_n=\\mathbb B^{\\mathbb B^n}\\)</span>, as in <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"5d10aed668d85817\" href=\"?note=5d10aed668d85817\" title=\"27-df-boolfunc\">27-df-boolfunc</a>.</li>\n<li>For <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"a,b\\in\\mathbb B^n\">\\(a,b\\in\\mathbb B^n\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"a\\preceq b\">\\(a\\preceq b\\)</span> means <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\forall i\\in[n]\\,(a_i\\le b_i)\">\\(\\forall i\\in[n]\\,(a_i\\le b_i)\\)</span>; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(a\\wedge b)_i=\\min(a_i,b_i)\">\\((a\\wedge b)_i=\\min(a_i,b_i)\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(a\\vee b)_i=\\max(a_i,b_i)\">\\((a\\vee b)_i=\\max(a_i,b_i)\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Monotone}_n\">\\(\\mathrm{Monotone}_n\\)</span> is the increasing class defined in <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"640eb8f2fbffd9d9\" href=\"?note=640eb8f2fbffd9d9\" title=\"27-df-monotone\">27-df-monotone</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\forall f\\in\\mathrm{BoolFunc}_n\\;\\left(f\\in\\mathrm{Monotone}_n\\;\\leftrightarrow\\;\\forall a,b\\in\\mathbb B^n\\;(a\\preceq b\\to f(a)\\le f(b))\\right).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\forall f\\in\\mathrm{BoolFunc}_n\\;\\left(f\\in\\mathrm{Monotone}_n\\;\\leftrightarrow\\;\\forall a,b\\in\\mathbb B^n\\;(a\\preceq b\\to f(a)\\le f(b))\\right).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>来源：Crama–Hammer (2011), §1.10.1, Theorem 1.20，印刷页 35，PDF 第 59 页（从 1 计数）。 已核对逐个提升坐标的证明。本目录按该序性质定义 Monotone_n，因此此节点同时是定义展开；书中名称是 positive。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"27-df-monotone","status":"resolved","id":"640eb8f2fbffd9d9","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[27-df-monotone]]","embed":false},{"target":"27-df-boolfunc","status":"resolved","id":"5d10aed668d85817","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$n\\in\\mathbb N$, $[n]=\\{1,\\ldots,n\\}$; $\\mathbb B=\\{0,1\\}$ and $\\mathrm{BoolFunc}_n=\\mathbb B^{\\mathbb B^n}$, as in [[27-df-boolfunc]].","embed":false},{"target":"27-df-monotone","status":"resolved","id":"640eb8f2fbffd9d9","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Monotone}_n$ is the increasing class defined in [[27-df-monotone]].","embed":false}],"attachments":[],"math":[{"tex":"n\\in\\mathbb N","display":false},{"tex":"[n]=\\{1,\\ldots,n\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb B=\\{0,1\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{BoolFunc}_n=\\mathbb B^{\\mathbb B^n}","display":false},{"tex":"a,b\\in\\mathbb B^n","display":false},{"tex":"a\\preceq b","display":false},{"tex":"\\forall i\\in[n]\\,(a_i\\le b_i)","display":false},{"tex":"(a\\wedge b)_i=\\min(a_i,b_i)","display":false},{"tex":"(a\\vee b)_i=\\max(a_i,b_i)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Monotone}_n","display":false},{"tex":"\\forall f\\in\\mathrm{BoolFunc}_n\\;\\left(f\\in\\mathrm{Monotone}_n\\;\\leftrightarrow\\;\\forall a,b\\in\\mathbb B^n\\;(a\\preceq b\\to f(a)\\le f(b))\\right).","display":true}],"bytes":1127,"backlinks":[{"id":"5244dbb38da17b8a","anchor":"ref-512","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[27-thm-poschar|thm-poschar — Order characterization of positivity]]"}],"outgoing":["640eb8f2fbffd9d9","5d10aed668d85817"]}